From: Kurcide <contact@aevonix.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Optional online FP8 for attention, shared experts and linear attention

Converts selected backbone linear layers to FP8 at load time from the bf16
checkpoint, with no checkpoint conversion and no extra files. Off unless
DRAMA3_BACKBONE_FP8=1, and the selection is DRAMA3_BACKBONE_FP8_SCOPE, a comma
list of attention, shared_experts and linear_attn.

The routed experts are already block-FP8 in the shipped checkpoint, so most of
the model's weight mass is FP8 before this patch does anything. What is left in
bf16 is the backbone, and converting it buys decode throughput rather than
memory: measured on one GB10, decode goes 28.58 -> 38.85 tok/s and TTFB 0.42 ->
0.36 s, for 1.309 GiB of weights saved and a load-time peak that RISES, because
the conversion happens after the bf16 weights are resident.

Two things worth knowing before changing the scope table.

The suffixes are RUNTIME module names, not checkpoint tensor names. The two
differ wherever upstream fuses projections, so a scope written from checkpoint
names selects nothing, serves perfectly, and reads as a result. The conversion
summary is logged for exactly that reason: check the module counts before
believing a measurement.

Three things are excluded on purpose and cannot be selected by any scope: the
MoE router and the shared-expert gate, because a small logit shift changes which
experts run at all; the linear-attention in_proj_ba, because it produces decay
and gating terms rather than a value path and so carries the precision risk of
the whole family for 0.4% of its bytes; and the linear-attention conv1d, which
upstream builds with quant_config=None so this config is never consulted for it.
